  "result": "Perfect! All 155 tests pass. I've successfully added payment terms support to createInvoice:\n\n**Changes to createInvoice:**\n\n1. **New parameter: `terms`** (optional, defaults to `'NET30'`)\n   - Accepts: `'NET14'`, `'NET30'`, `'EOM'`\n   - Returns `TERMS_INVALID` for unknown values\n\n2. **Automatic due date calculation** based on terms:\n   - `'NET14'`: issueDate + 14 days\n   - `'NET30'`: issueDate + 30 days\n   - `'EOM'`: Last day of the issue month\n\n3. **Invoice structure updated** to include:\n   - `invoice.terms`: The payment term type\n   - `invoice.dueDate`: The calculated due date (YYYY-MM-DD format)\n\n4. **Terms and dueDate are preserved** through:\n   - `addLine()` modifications\n   - `removeLine()` modifications\n   - `issueInvoice()` when issued\n\n5. **New error code added:**\n   - `TERMS_INVALID`: Invalid or unknown term type\n\n**Test coverage includes:**\n- Default NET30 behavior\n- All three term types (NET14, NET30, EOM)\n- Edge cases: month boundaries, year boundaries, leap year February\n- Invalid term rejection\n\nAll invoice functions now properly track and preserve payment terms throughout their lifecycle. \u2714",
